---
title: Topics
description: Browse every post on ReverentGeek by topic — from Node.js and databases to sketchnoting, public speaking, and motorcycles.
layout: layouts/default.edge
---
<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mt-4 mb-2">Browse by Topic</h1>
<p class="text-gray-600 mb-8">
  All {{ collections.posts.length }} posts, sorted into the things I keep coming back to.
  Read the <a class="underline text-action" href="/#latest-writing">latest posts</a>
  or the <a class="underline text-action" href="/archive/">full archive</a> by year.
</p>

{{-- Hidden until index.js wires it up, so there's no dead search box without JavaScript. --}}
<div class="post-search" data-post-search hidden>
  <label class="post-search-label" for="post-search-input">Search posts</label>
  <input class="post-search-input" id="post-search-input" type="search" autocomplete="off"
    placeholder="Try “teleprompter”, “Electron”, or “speaking”" aria-describedby="post-search-status">
  <p class="post-search-status" id="post-search-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <ul class="post-search-results" data-post-search-results></ul>
</div>

<div class="topic-list mb-12">
  @each(topic in collections.topics)
    @!component('components/topic-chip', { slug: topic.slug, count: topic.count })
  @end
</div>

<p class="text-gray-600">
  Looking for something specific? The <a class="underline text-action" href="/archive/">full archive</a>
  lists every post by year, or grab the <a class="underline text-action" href="/feed.xml">RSS feed</a>.
</p>
